// Title: Chromium Browser Headless Execution To Mockbin Like Site
// Sigma ID: 1c526788-0abe-4713-862f-b520da5e5316
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: X__Junior (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-09-11 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution
// Description: Detects the execution of a Chromium based browser process with the "headless" flag and a URL
//   pointing to the mockbin.org service (which can be used to exfiltrate data).
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.zscaler.com/blogs/security-research/steal-it-campaign
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_browsers_chromium_mockbin_abuse.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\brave.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\chrome.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\msedge.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\opera.exe" or FolderPath endswith "\\vivaldi.exe") and ProcessCommandLine contains "--headless" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "://run.mocky" or ProcessCommandLine contains "://mockbin")
